From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: il97680a: expose a luminance-linear backlight scale

The DDIC drives the panel at luminance ~ (DBV/3445)^2.4, measured on the
Retroid Pocket Nova module. Raw DBV in sysfs compresses the useful
brightness range into the top of the scale and collapses the low end
under nits-based brightness control. Translate the now luminance-linear
sysfs scale to DBV through the brightness levels helper and declare
BACKLIGHT_SCALE_LINEAR. Report the cached brightness instead of reading
the register back so the reported value stays in scale units.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c	2026-08-29 18:22:22.108668614 -0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ilitek-il97680a.c	2026-08-29 18:46:25.920796598 -0400
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 
 	struct gpio_desc *reset_gpio;
 	struct regulator_bulk_data *supplies;
+	struct drm_panel_bl_levels bl_levels;
 };
 
 struct panel_desc {
@@ -285,10 +286,55 @@
 	.get_orientation = il97680a_get_orientation,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The DDIC drives the panel at luminance ~ (DBV/3445)^2.4, measured on the
+ * Retroid Pocket Nova module. Userspace brightness models assume a scale
+ * linear in luminance, so the sysfs value is linear light, mapped to DBV
+ * through these levels.
+ */
